{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Like the garden of YHWH, like the land of Egypt</b> — he says that the entire land of the plain is watered by foot from the Jordan, in the manner done in the garden of YHWH, concerning which it is stated (Genesis 2:10), \"And a river went out from Eden to water the garden,\" and in the manner it is in the land of Egypt, concerning which it is stated (Deuteronomy 11:10), \"and you watered it with your foot, like a garden of greens.\" And He mentioned two places: He said \"like the garden of YHWH,\" for the choicest place among the lowlands is thus entirely irrigated, and He mentioned \"like the land of Egypt,\" a place known for pasturage. And our Sages said (Sifrei Ekev 38), \"Like the garden of YHWH\" for the trees, \"like the land of Egypt\" for the seeds. They mean to explain that in the plain there are great rivers that water the trees of the orchards like the garden of YHWH, and in it there are channels like the land of Egypt that water the garden of greens. And Lot chose this for himself, for a land watered in this manner is distant from drought and good for pasture."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:27:59.336423063Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}